WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Your spine is a stack
of bones: 7 in the neck,

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.200
12 in the chest, 5 in the lower back.

3
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.960
Pick up one from the neck.

4
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.060
It is small and light.

5
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.250
Now pick up one from the lower back.

6
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.770
It is huge by comparison.

7
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.720
So why are the bones in your neck small,
but the ones in your lower back huge?

8
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.780
In this mission, you'll
split the skeleton in two:

9
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.730
the central axis, and the limbs
and girdles attached to it.

10
00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.110
Then you'll take one vertebra
apart: its solid body,

11
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.630
the arch around the spinal cord,
and the spines that anchor muscles.

12
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: explain why
your neck vertebrae are small,

13
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.480
but your lower-back ones are huge.
